<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karlsruhe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1715">1715</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karlsruhe is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, founded in 1715 by Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-william-margrave-of-baden-durlach">Charles III William</a> of Baden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durlach">Durlach</a> as a new residence. It was planned in a fan shape, with streets radiating from the palace tower. It was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> until 1945 and is now the seat of Germany's Federal Constitutional Court and Federal Court of Justice.</p></div>
